# NEVER commit state — it holds every attribute AWS returned, including
# secrets, in plaintext. If it reaches a public repo, rotate everything in it.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Provider binaries — hundreds of MB, re-downloadable by `terraform init`
.terraform/

# Your real values — often an IP, a key name, sometimes worse
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

crash.log
crash.*.log

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is NOT ignored, on purpose.
# It pins the exact provider versions the whole team resolves to — it is a
# lockfile, same idea as package-lock.json. Commit it.
